Z||000007||ur2biteme||01-22-2001||03:38 AM||||my late stepdad (great guy, miss him dearly) was restoring a '58 fury to show quality.  painted it red and was gonna restore it to basically be that car.  it was kinda eerie walking into that garage alone sometimes.  especially when i used to live in manteca where my mom and stepdad lived originally.  the washer and dryer were right in front of it.  if you didnt watch it, you'd bump right into that huge chrome bumper while doing laundry.  all i would have needed is someone hiding in the car to flip on the brights real quick while i was doing laundry in the dark to make me crap my pants.  lol.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A> <p>[This message has been edited by ur2biteme (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
